@prompt
The garden keeps a log. Text comes apart with string functions, and `string_match` tests a pattern against a string (a small regex). The Task Reference sidebar has a brief regex guide.

# Task
Keep only the log entries that mention a bloom. Fill the test so `filter` keeps the entries containing `"bloom"`.

@hint
Use `string_match(pattern, e)` to test each entry.

@reference
### Strings
- `string_match(pattern, s)` is `true` if the pattern occurs in `s`. Patterns are regexes, e.g. `"bloom"` or `"#[0-9]+"`.
- `string_split(" ", s)` breaks `s` into pieces
- `string_length(s)`, `string_sub(s, start, len)`

@hints
Keep "moonbloom ok" and "starbloom ok".

@code
let entries = ["moonbloom ok", "cactus dry", "starbloom ok"] in
filter(entries, fun e ->
¿
